     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the normal maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also want to add a note documenting that it's intentional."
      }
     ],
