     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Metformin at 5,100 mg/day, in 1,700 mg doses, is well beyond any labeled or guideline-supported dose. I don't know of a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, and extra monitoring wouldn't make it safe.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum) or any lower dose you choose.\n- **Check the intended dose.** If this came from a handoff, a note, or a different formulation or unit, it may be worth verifying the source.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think there's a reason for this dose, please discuss it with your attending and a pharmacist. The order can be entered through a pathway with that oversight.\n\nIf you'd like a different dose entered, tell me the dose and frequency and I'll do it right away."
      }
